    <item>
      <title>Silence is Loud</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/music_blog/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 15 Feb 2026 15:15:00 +0530</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/music_blog/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;welcome-to-my-blog&#34;&gt;Welcome to my Blog!&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;intro&#34;&gt;Intro&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As I write this, I have made a conscious decision to quit listening to music for 6 months.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You might ask: Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To be honest, I have been addicted. For the last two years, I’ve had headphones on constantly—while traveling, walking, and even during &amp;ldquo;focused&amp;rdquo; work. I was listening to music a lot. A lot.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The worst part wasn&amp;rsquo;t just the volume; it was the content. My consumption became repetitive, looping the same tracks hundreds of times. My taste progressively worsened, shifting toward sped-up, high-dopamine TikTok edits designed to hack my attention. I realized the lyrics and beats were hijacking my emotions and dictating my mood. My mind was in an altered state whenever the headphones were on.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>About Me</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/about/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 11 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/about/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I’m a final-year Computer Science student at PES University and currently an AI Intern at Tvam Technologies. My current work focuses on fine-tuning language models, and I’m deeply fascinated by how AI can be applied to solve meaningful real-world problems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As I grow in this field, I aim to advance from fine-tuning existing models to building my own. I’m always looking for opportunities to strengthen my skills, take on new challenges, and contribute to impactful projects. I also have a growing interest in Big Data and Database Systems, helping me build a strong and versatile technical foundation. Outside of technology, I enjoy capturing moments through photography and love the strategic challenge of chess.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>AI Intern @ Tvam Technologies</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/experience/tvam/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/experience/tvam/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h3 id=&#34;role-overview&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Intern&lt;/strong&gt; | &lt;em&gt;Sept 2025 – Present&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am currently an AI Intern at Tvam Technologies, responsible for fine-tuning language models and adapting them to the company’s unique needs and applications. As I progress in my role, I will also be working on creating and training new models.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;current-responsibilities&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Fine-tuning language models using PEFT, LoRA, and hyperparameter tuning.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Preparing and preprocessing datasets: curation, cleaning, formatting, and prompt creation.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Designing custom data workflows to improve downstream model performance.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Conducting research through papers, articles, and benchmarks to guide experiments.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Strengthening fundamentals by learning Python from scratch through books and practice.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Preparing clear reports and documentation for experiments and results.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Planning to expand into model creation and architecture design as the internship progresses.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
